A machete’s trade does not kill the machete; a hoe’s trade does not cause problems for the hoe.

- Òwò àdá kì í pa àdá; òwò ọkọ́ kì í yọ ọkọ́ lẹ́nu

[0] "In the event of a machete trade, a machete will never pay for itself"; 
[1] "A hoe can never have a trade disagreement with a hoe"; 
[2] "If a machete goes into trade with a hoe, neither will suffer financially"

[kí ó rọ̀ wá, àyè pọ̀ sí ọ̀nà; 
ó sọ̀rọ̀ òun ṣẹ̀rè gbé; 
ó ni yóò rọ̀ wá ẹyin.]

[
  "You will not find shade to protect you from the sun by going this way.",
